1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,629
May 2022.

2
00:00:00,629 --> 00:00:06,850
In just a few days, a cryptocurrency worth around 40
billion dollars falls to almost zero.

3
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:13,141
Its price had been above 100 dollars only a month
earlier. Now it's worth less than a cent.

4
00:00:13,691 --> 00:00:17,578
In apartments across Seoul, in Singapore,
in the United States,

5
00:00:17,578 --> 00:00:22,243
hundreds of thousands of people watch
their savings disappear in real time.

6
00:00:22,243 --> 00:00:25,466
Many of them had been told this was the
safe option.

7
00:00:26,466 --> 00:00:29,602
The man behind it had once mocked his
critics online.

8
00:00:29,602 --> 00:00:34,573
A year later, he would be arrested at an airport in
the Balkans with a fake passport.

9
00:00:34,823 --> 00:00:38,548
And years after that, standing in a New
York courtroom,

10
00:00:38,548 --> 00:00:43,762
he would finally admit what really happened the
first time his coin nearly died.

11
00:00:43,762 --> 00:00:45,881
This is the story of Terra-Luna.

12
00:00:47,381 --> 00:00:51,796
Do Kwon grew up in Seoul, studied computer
science at Stanford,

13
00:00:51,796 --> 00:00:56,211
and worked briefly as a software engineer
at Microsoft and Apple.

14
00:00:56,211 --> 00:01:02,834
Then he came home. In 2016, he started a small wireless
networking company in Korea called Anyfi.

15
00:01:03,084 --> 00:01:06,372
It was a modest startup. What came next
was not.

16
00:01:06,922 --> 00:01:11,996
In early 2018, Kwon co-founded Terraform
Labs with Daniel Shin,

17
00:01:11,996 --> 00:01:15,041
one of Korea's best-known startup
founders.

18
00:01:15,041 --> 00:01:18,181
Shin had built Ticket Monster, or TMON,

19
00:01:18,181 --> 00:01:24,462
one of the country's big e-commerce platforms, and
he knew merchants all over Korea.

20
00:01:24,712 --> 00:01:28,575
The pairing made sense. Kwon had the code.
Shin had the customers.

21
00:01:29,125 --> 00:01:31,201
Kwon also had something else:

22
00:01:31,201 --> 00:01:36,597
a voice. On Twitter, he was sharp, funny,
and supremely sure of himself.

23
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:41,120
By 2022, around a million people followed
him. To many of them,

24
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:44,513
he wasn't just a founder. He was the
future.

25
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:47,983
Terra's big idea was a stablecoin.

26
00:01:47,983 --> 00:01:52,234
Most cryptocurrencies swing wildly in
price. A stablecoin

27
00:01:52,234 --> 00:01:56,485
is supposed to stay at one dollar. Always.

28
00:01:56,485 --> 00:02:01,810
That stability is what lets people use
crypto like real money.

29
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:05,781
Most stablecoins do this the boring way.
For every coin,

30
00:02:05,781 --> 00:02:09,545
they hold a real dollar, or something like
it, in reserve.

31
00:02:09,545 --> 00:02:10,364
Terra didn't.

32
00:02:11,564 --> 00:02:15,762
But before we look at how Terra worked,
you need to see how it was sold.

33
00:02:15,762 --> 00:02:20,952
Because in the beginning, the pitch wasn't about
getting rich. It was about buying coffee.

34
00:02:21,502 --> 00:02:26,985
In 2019, Shin's other company launched a
mobile payments app in Korea called Chai.

35
00:02:26,985 --> 00:02:32,401
Shoppers got discounts. Merchants paid lower fees
than the card companies charged.

36
00:02:32,651 --> 00:02:38,747
And Terra told the world that, behind the scenes, those
payments were running on the Terra blockchain.

37
00:02:39,297 --> 00:02:45,634
Terra didn't only have a dollar coin. It also had a coin
pegged to the Korean won, called KRT.

38
00:02:45,884 --> 00:02:52,292
In 2019, Chai partnered with Terraform to bring that
won coin into its app. Every coffee,

39
00:02:52,292 --> 00:02:58,300
every online order, was supposed to be a
tiny proof that Terra worked as money.

40
00:02:58,850 --> 00:03:05,518
Terra's own announcements boasted of hundreds of
thousands of users and millions of transactions.

41
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:08,575
For investors, this was the killer
argument.

42
00:03:08,575 --> 00:03:13,409
Most crypto projects were just promises.
Terra could point to real people,

43
00:03:13,409 --> 00:03:16,632
in a real country, paying for real things.

44
00:03:17,632 --> 00:03:22,460
Keep the name Chai in mind. It comes back
later in this story. In a courtroom.

45
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:25,113
Terra had two coins.

46
00:03:25,113 --> 00:03:28,600
UST, the stablecoin meant to stay at one
dollar.

47
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:32,887
And LUNA, its sister coin, whose price
could rise and fall.

48
00:03:33,437 --> 00:03:39,522
The system promised that you could always swap one UST
for one dollar's worth of LUNA, and back.

49
00:03:39,522 --> 00:03:43,173
If UST dropped below a dollar, traders
could buy it cheap,

50
00:03:43,173 --> 00:03:46,824
swap it for a dollar of LUNA, and pocket
the difference.

51
00:03:47,074 --> 00:03:51,253
In theory, that buying pressure would push
UST back to a dollar. Forever.

52
00:03:51,803 --> 00:03:53,917
Here's what that looks like.

53
00:03:53,917 --> 00:03:59,798
Say UST slips to 97 cents. You buy one.
You hand it to the system,

54
00:03:59,798 --> 00:04:06,072
which destroys it, and gives you one dollar's worth of
brand-new LUNA. You've made three cents.

55
00:04:06,322 --> 00:04:11,073
Thousands of traders doing that at once
remove UST from circulation,

56
00:04:11,073 --> 00:04:14,528
until the price climbs back to a dollar.

57
00:04:14,528 --> 00:04:21,063
And if UST goes above a dollar, it works the other
way: burn LUNA, create UST, sell it.

58
00:04:22,063 --> 00:04:26,095
There was no vault of dollars behind it.
Just code, and confidence.

59
00:04:26,095 --> 00:04:31,450
And the whole thing depended on one assumption: that
LUNA would always be worth something.

60
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:37,874
Critics called it what it looked like: a design that could
spiral to zero if confidence ever broke.

61
00:04:37,874 --> 00:04:41,230
Kwon's response to critics was famous for
its arrogance.

62
00:04:41,230 --> 00:04:46,505
When one of them challenged him online, he replied:
"I don't debate the poor on Twitter."

63
00:04:47,705 --> 00:04:49,085
Then came the bait.

64
00:04:49,085 --> 00:04:51,791
A lending platform built on Terra,

65
00:04:51,791 --> 00:04:57,653
called Anchor Protocol, offered close to 20 percent
annual interest on UST deposits.

66
00:04:57,903 --> 00:05:01,620
Your bank was offering almost nothing.
Anchor offered nearly 20 percent,

67
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:06,012
on a coin that was supposed to be as
stable as a dollar.

68
00:05:06,562 --> 00:05:07,880
Money poured in.

69
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:11,917
By early 2022, the vast majority of all
UST

70
00:05:11,917 --> 00:05:15,954
in existence was sitting in Anchor,
earning that yield.

71
00:05:15,954 --> 00:05:19,568
LUNA's price soared above 100 dollars.
Terra's

72
00:05:19,568 --> 00:05:23,699
total value reached tens of billions of
dollars.

73
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:28,726
Terraform even signed a five-year
sponsorship deal with the

74
00:05:28,726 --> 00:05:34,034
Washington Nationals baseball team,
reported at about 38 million dollars.

75
00:05:34,034 --> 00:05:40,376
In Korea, Kwon was hailed as a crypto genius. His
fans called themselves "Lunatics."

76
00:05:41,376 --> 00:05:44,904
But where was that 20 percent actually
coming from?

77
00:05:44,904 --> 00:05:48,079
For a long time, the honest answer was:

78
00:05:48,079 --> 00:05:52,445
largely from Terra itself, subsidizing the
payments to keep people in.

79
00:05:52,995 --> 00:05:59,389
Anchor kept a reserve to cover the gap between what
borrowers paid and what depositors were promised.

80
00:05:59,389 --> 00:06:04,377
By early 2022, that reserve was draining
by more than a million dollars a day.

81
00:06:04,627 --> 00:06:11,584
So in February 2022, the Luna Foundation Guard, an
organization we'll meet properly in a minute,

82
00:06:11,584 --> 00:06:18,976
approved a top-up of 450 million dollars' worth of
UST, just to keep the 20 percent going.

83
00:06:19,226 --> 00:06:22,800
Shortly after, Anchor's community voted to
let the rate slowly come

84
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:26,374
down. But by then, the promise had already
done its work.

85
00:06:27,574 --> 00:06:32,040
Here's the twist most people never heard
at the time.

86
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:36,116
In May 2021, a year before the final
collapse,

87
00:06:36,116 --> 00:06:39,286
UST had already lost its one-dollar peg.

88
00:06:39,286 --> 00:06:42,403
And then, mysteriously, it recovered.

89
00:06:42,953 --> 00:06:46,876
The public story was that the code worked.
The algorithm fixed itself.

90
00:06:46,876 --> 00:06:50,015
But years later, U.S. regulators told a
different story.

91
00:06:50,265 --> 00:06:55,189
According to the SEC, the recovery was
driven by a large trading

92
00:06:55,189 --> 00:07:00,523
firm quietly buying UST behind the scenes,
under a secret deal with Terraform.

93
00:07:01,073 --> 00:07:04,727
The SEC's account goes like this. On May
23,

94
00:07:04,727 --> 00:07:09,600
2021, as UST slid, Terraform made a verbal
agreement with the firm.

95
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:16,130
Terraform would loosen the restrictions on the
firm's right to buy LUNA at a discount.

96
00:07:16,380 --> 00:07:20,492
In return, according to the SEC, the firm
bought more than

97
00:07:20,492 --> 00:07:24,604
20 million dollars of UST to push the
price back up.

98
00:07:24,604 --> 00:07:31,034
The SEC said that investors were misled into
believing the algorithm had saved the peg.

99
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:37,301
The trading firm's affiliate later settled with the SEC
without admitting or denying the claims.

100
00:07:38,301 --> 00:07:42,066
If that's true, the system hadn't passed
its stress

101
00:07:42,066 --> 00:07:46,250
test. It had been rescued. And the rescue
was hidden.

102
00:07:46,250 --> 00:07:51,601
So who knew? And would anyone ever admit
it? Hold on to that question.

103
00:07:52,801 --> 00:07:59,074
By early 2022, the warnings were getting
louder. Kwon's answer was a war chest.

104
00:07:59,074 --> 00:08:05,823
In January 2022, a nonprofit called the Luna
Foundation Guard was set up in Singapore.

105
00:08:05,823 --> 00:08:11,778
Its job was to build a reserve that could
defend UST's peg in an emergency.

106
00:08:12,028 --> 00:08:16,057
Kwon said the goal was 10 billion dollars'
worth of bitcoin.

107
00:08:16,607 --> 00:08:23,194
The first big chunk of money came in February: a
one-billion-dollar sale of LUNA to investors,

108
00:08:23,194 --> 00:08:29,781
led by two heavyweight crypto firms, Jump Crypto and a
hedge fund called Three Arrows Capital.

109
00:08:29,781 --> 00:08:32,951
Remember that second name. It comes back
too.

110
00:08:33,501 --> 00:08:36,657
And it bought fast. On some days that
spring,

111
00:08:36,657 --> 00:08:41,215
it was buying more than 100 million
dollars of bitcoin at a time.

112
00:08:41,215 --> 00:08:47,596
Kwon said he expected to reach the 10-billion-dollar
target by the end of the third quarter.

113
00:08:47,846 --> 00:08:54,381
Anyone could watch the reserve wallets
fill up on the blockchain, in real time.

114
00:08:54,381 --> 00:08:59,882
By early May, it held 80,394 bitcoin,
worth around 2.4 billion dollars.

115
00:08:59,882 --> 00:09:05,383
It had become one of the biggest bitcoin
holders in the world.

116
00:09:05,633 --> 00:09:09,483
To many investors, this looked like the
missing

117
00:09:09,483 --> 00:09:13,814
piece. The vault Terra never had, finally
being filled.

118
00:09:14,814 --> 00:09:16,357
But there was a catch.

119
00:09:16,357 --> 00:09:22,110
The reserve was a fraction of the nearly
19 billion dollars of UST in circulation.

120
00:09:22,110 --> 00:09:28,283
And it was held in bitcoin, an asset that could fall
at exactly the moment it was needed.

121
00:09:28,533 --> 00:09:32,404
U.S. prosecutors later said there was
another problem:

122
00:09:32,404 --> 00:09:39,661
Kwon presented the foundation as independent from Terraform,
when, according to prosecutors, he controlled it.

123
00:09:40,211 --> 00:09:45,041
So before we watch the fall, here are two
questions to carry with you.

124
00:09:45,041 --> 00:09:48,353
Was the 2021 rescue really hidden from
investors?

125
00:09:48,353 --> 00:09:52,079
And were those Chai payments really
running on Terra?

126
00:09:52,329 --> 00:09:58,029
Both get answered before the end of this video. One by
a jury. The other by Do Kwon himself.

127
00:09:59,229 --> 00:10:00,917
Saturday, May 7, 2022.

128
00:10:00,917 --> 00:10:05,289
Anchor is holding about 14 billion
dollars' worth of UST.

129
00:10:05,289 --> 00:10:10,314
Terraform pulls a large amount of UST out
of a key trading pool on

130
00:10:10,314 --> 00:10:15,338
a platform called Curve, as part of a
planned move to a new pool.

131
00:10:15,588 --> 00:10:22,458
Within minutes, other wallets dump tens of
millions of UST into what's left.

132
00:10:22,458 --> 00:10:25,894
The pool tilts. UST slips to 99 cents.

133
00:10:25,894 --> 00:10:31,819
It sounds tiny. It isn't. For a coin whose
whole promise is one dollar,

134
00:10:31,819 --> 00:10:35,205
a penny is a crack in the glass.

135
00:10:35,755 --> 00:10:39,752
Sunday. Anchor depositors head for the
exit. Billions of

136
00:10:39,752 --> 00:10:43,748
dollars of UST leave in a matter of days.

137
00:10:43,748 --> 00:10:48,486
The Luna Foundation Guard says it will
lend 1.5 billion dollars,

138
00:10:48,486 --> 00:10:53,224
half in bitcoin and half in UST, to defend
the peg.

139
00:10:53,474 --> 00:10:57,421
Kwon tweets: "Deploying more capital.
Steady lads."

140
00:10:57,971 --> 00:11:00,694
Monday. The defense isn't working.

141
00:11:00,694 --> 00:11:04,978
The foundation's bitcoin starts leaving
its wallets to

142
00:11:04,978 --> 00:11:09,263
be sold. Bitcoin itself slides toward
30,000 dollars.

143
00:11:09,263 --> 00:11:13,899
Anchor deposits fall from 14 billion to
under 9 billion. UST,

144
00:11:13,899 --> 00:11:17,271
at one point, drops to around 35 cents.

145
00:11:17,821 --> 00:11:20,826
And now the magic trick runs in reverse.

146
00:11:20,826 --> 00:11:25,108
To defend the peg, the system creates more
and more LUNA.

147
00:11:25,108 --> 00:11:28,714
More LUNA means each LUNA is worth less.
Which

148
00:11:28,714 --> 00:11:32,320
means less trust in UST. Which means more
selling.

149
00:11:32,870 --> 00:11:37,441
Tuesday and Wednesday. Exchanges choke on
the flood of transactions.

150
00:11:37,441 --> 00:11:42,469
The world's largest exchange, Binance,
briefly pauses LUNA and UST withdrawals.

151
00:11:42,469 --> 00:11:47,693
LUNA, worth around 80 dollars at the start
of the month, falls below one dollar.

152
00:11:48,243 --> 00:11:53,456
The supply of LUNA explodes from hundreds
of millions of coins into the trillions.

153
00:11:54,006 --> 00:11:59,818
Thursday. The Terra blockchain itself is halted. By
Friday, it has been halted again.

154
00:11:59,818 --> 00:12:06,115
Major exchanges pull LUNA and UST from trading. LUNA is
now worth a tiny fraction of a cent.

155
00:12:06,365 --> 00:12:12,704
That Friday, Kwon writes: "I am heartbroken about the pain
my invention has brought on all of you."

156
00:12:13,254 --> 00:12:16,900
The following Monday, the Luna Foundation
Guard says

157
00:12:16,900 --> 00:12:20,545
it has 313 bitcoin left. Out of 80,394.

158
00:12:20,545 --> 00:12:24,752
An audit the foundation released later put
the total

159
00:12:24,752 --> 00:12:28,958
spent defending the peg at about 2.8
billion dollars.

160
00:12:29,958 --> 00:12:34,739
Around 40 billion dollars of value, gone
in a matter of days.

161
00:12:34,739 --> 00:12:40,853
Some victims had put in their life savings. Many
had trusted the word "stable."

162
00:12:42,053 --> 00:12:43,736
Who were the Lunatics?

163
00:12:43,736 --> 00:12:47,444
In Korea, they gathered in group chat
rooms

164
00:12:47,444 --> 00:12:51,616
and online forums. Overseas, on Reddit,
Discord and Twitter.

165
00:12:51,616 --> 00:12:54,208
For two years, they shared memes,

166
00:12:54,208 --> 00:12:58,960
price targets, and a kind of belonging.
Kwon was their captain.

167
00:12:59,510 --> 00:13:01,396
Many of them weren't gamblers.

168
00:13:01,396 --> 00:13:06,740
The stories posted online came from office workers,
retirees, young couples saving for a home,

169
00:13:06,740 --> 00:13:12,084
people who had moved money out of a bank
because Anchor paid many times more.

170
00:13:12,634 --> 00:13:17,649
After the crash, those same communities
changed overnight. The memes stopped.

171
00:13:17,649 --> 00:13:24,487
Moderators of the biggest English-language forum pinned links
to support helplines at the top of the page.

172
00:13:24,737 --> 00:13:29,334
In Korea, where LUNA had traded on the
country's biggest exchanges,

173
00:13:29,334 --> 00:13:31,842
those exchanges moved to delist it.

174
00:13:31,842 --> 00:13:38,111
Groups of Korean investors filed criminal complaints
and lawsuits against Terra's founders.

175
00:13:39,111 --> 00:13:44,373
We are not naming any of them here. Their
losses are not entertainment.

176
00:13:44,373 --> 00:13:50,820
But every number in this story was somebody's rent,
somebody's savings, somebody's plan.

177
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:53,955
Terra did not fall alone.

178
00:13:53,955 --> 00:14:00,922
Remember Three Arrows Capital, the Singapore-based hedge fund
that helped lead that billion-dollar LUNA sale? It

179
00:14:00,922 --> 00:14:07,888
had made a large bet on LUNA. When LUNA
went to zero, so did the bet.

180
00:14:08,138 --> 00:14:13,524
By the start of July, a court in the British Virgin
Islands had ordered the fund liquidated.

181
00:14:14,074 --> 00:14:16,891
The firms that had lent to it were next.

182
00:14:16,891 --> 00:14:21,293
Voyager Digital, which said Three Arrows
had defaulted on a loan

183
00:14:21,293 --> 00:14:25,695
of about 650 million dollars, filed for
bankruptcy on July 5.

184
00:14:25,945 --> 00:14:30,593
Celsius Network, a crypto lender that had
promised its users high yields,

185
00:14:30,593 --> 00:14:34,854
froze withdrawals in June and filed for
bankruptcy on July 13.

186
00:14:35,404 --> 00:14:37,351
And then there was FTX.

187
00:14:37,601 --> 00:14:44,256
At the criminal trial of FTX founder Sam Bankman-Fried, a
former top executive of his trading firm,

188
00:14:44,256 --> 00:14:50,519
Alameda Research, testified that after the crash, lenders
started demanding their money back in June 2022,

189
00:14:50,519 --> 00:14:55,216
and that Alameda repaid them using money
that came from FTX customers.

190
00:14:55,466 --> 00:15:01,959
FTX collapsed in November 2022. Bankman-Fried was
convicted of fraud a year later.

191
00:15:02,959 --> 00:15:07,482
Terra didn't commit FTX's fraud. A jury
put that on Bankman-Fried.

192
00:15:07,482 --> 00:15:11,170
But according to that testimony, the panic
that began in

193
00:15:11,170 --> 00:15:15,226
May was part of what pushed customer money
into the hole.

194
00:15:16,426 --> 00:15:20,897
While the dominoes fell, Kwon proposed a
fix: start over.

195
00:15:20,897 --> 00:15:27,251
On May 25, Terra's community voted for a
new blockchain. On May 28, it went live.

196
00:15:27,501 --> 00:15:32,826
The new coin was also called LUNA. The old
chain was renamed Terra Classic,

197
00:15:32,826 --> 00:15:36,250
and the old coins became LUNA Classic and
USTC.

198
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:43,301
Holders of the old coins received airdrops of new
LUNA, based on what they held and when.

199
00:15:43,301 --> 00:15:47,142
One thing was missing. There was no new
UST.

200
00:15:47,142 --> 00:15:50,984
Terra 2.0 launched without an algorithmic
stablecoin at all.

201
00:15:51,234 --> 00:15:57,432
The new LUNA briefly traded above 17 dollars, then quickly
fell as people sold what they'd been given.

202
00:15:57,432 --> 00:16:01,175
For many old holders, it was nowhere near
what they had lost.

203
00:16:02,375 --> 00:16:06,351
When the collapse hit, Kwon was living in
Singapore.

204
00:16:06,351 --> 00:16:11,346
In September 2022, a Seoul court issued a
warrant for his arrest,

205
00:16:11,346 --> 00:16:13,844
and Interpol issued a red notice.

206
00:16:13,844 --> 00:16:19,120
He said he wasn't on the run. But nobody
seemed to know where he was.

207
00:16:19,370 --> 00:16:24,649
Days after the warrant, Singapore police
said he was no longer in Singapore.

208
00:16:24,649 --> 00:16:28,768
In October, Korea's foreign ministry
invalidated his passport. Online,

209
00:16:28,768 --> 00:16:32,429
he kept posting as if nothing had changed.

210
00:16:32,979 --> 00:16:35,891
In March 2023, at the airport in
Podgorica,

211
00:16:35,891 --> 00:16:40,987
the capital of Montenegro, police stopped
a man trying to board a private flight.

212
00:16:40,987 --> 00:16:43,958
He was carrying a forged Costa Rican
passport.

213
00:16:43,958 --> 00:16:44,927
It was Do Kwon.

214
00:16:45,177 --> 00:16:49,834
A Montenegrin court sentenced him to four
months in prison for the forged documents.

215
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:53,499
Both South Korea and the United States
wanted him.

216
00:16:53,499 --> 00:16:56,229
For more than a year and a half,

217
00:16:56,229 --> 00:17:01,349
Montenegro's courts and ministers went back and forth
over which country should get him first.

218
00:17:01,349 --> 00:17:06,084
In the end, he was extradited to the
United States, on the last day of 2024.

219
00:17:07,284 --> 00:17:13,783
America went after Kwon twice. Once in
civil court. Once in criminal court.

220
00:17:14,333 --> 00:17:17,165
The SEC sued Terraform and Kwon in
February 2023.

221
00:17:17,165 --> 00:17:22,483
Remember Chai? The SEC alleged that Chai's payments were not
actually processed on the Terra blockchain,

222
00:17:22,483 --> 00:17:27,801
and that transactions were copied onto the
chain to make it look as if they were.

223
00:17:28,051 --> 00:17:33,034
In April 2024, a jury in New York found
Terraform and Kwon liable for fraud.

224
00:17:33,034 --> 00:17:37,030
Afterwards, the SEC said the trial had
exposed the defendants'

225
00:17:37,030 --> 00:17:41,426
lies about the use of the Terra blockchain
to settle transactions.

226
00:17:41,676 --> 00:17:46,527
In June 2024, Terraform and Kwon agreed to
a settlement

227
00:17:46,527 --> 00:17:51,863
of about 4.47 billion dollars, and
Terraform agreed to wind down.

228
00:17:52,413 --> 00:17:56,325
Then came the criminal case. In August
2025,

229
00:17:56,325 --> 00:18:02,683
Kwon pleaded guilty to two fraud charges.
And in court, he said this:

230
00:18:02,683 --> 00:18:06,318
"In 2021, I made false and misleading

231
00:18:06,318 --> 00:18:09,953
statements about why UST regained its
peg."

232
00:18:10,953 --> 00:18:15,774
That was the hidden rescue. The question
from earlier, answered by the man himself.

233
00:18:16,324 --> 00:18:20,486
In December 2025, the judge sentenced him
to 15 years in

234
00:18:20,486 --> 00:18:25,026
prison. That was longer than the 12 years
prosecutors had asked for.

235
00:18:25,026 --> 00:18:29,307
The judge called it a fraud on an "epic,
generational scale."

236
00:18:30,507 --> 00:18:36,326
Most English coverage stops there. But the biggest
group of retail victims was in Korea.

237
00:18:36,326 --> 00:18:39,439
According to figures from Korean financial
authorities,

238
00:18:39,439 --> 00:18:43,885
about 280,000 people in Korea held LUNA
when it collapsed.

239
00:18:44,135 --> 00:18:50,532
Within days of the crash, Seoul prosecutors revived a
financial-crimes unit nicknamed the "Yeouido Grim

240
00:18:50,532 --> 00:18:57,356
Reaper," after the district where Korea's financial
industry lives. Terra was one of its first cases.

241
00:18:57,906 --> 00:19:03,216
In April 2023, Korean prosecutors indicted
Daniel Shin and several others.

242
00:19:03,216 --> 00:19:09,603
Prosecutors allege that Chai made ordinary payments
look as if they were running on Terra.

243
00:19:09,853 --> 00:19:13,348
Shin denies wrongdoing. His lawyers say he
left Terra two

244
00:19:13,348 --> 00:19:17,192
years before the collapse and had nothing
to do with it.

245
00:19:17,192 --> 00:19:22,842
Korean courts twice turned down requests to arrest
him, and his trial is still going on.

246
00:19:23,392 --> 00:19:26,470
And Do Kwon may not be done with Korean
justice.

247
00:19:26,470 --> 00:19:32,691
U.S. prosecutors said they would not oppose a transfer to
Korea after he serves half his sentence.

248
00:19:32,941 --> 00:19:38,317
In Korea, he would still face separate charges,
including under the capital markets law.

249
00:19:38,317 --> 00:19:44,077
Some Korean media have reported that a conviction
there could mean more than 30 years.

250
00:19:45,277 --> 00:19:49,119
Terra wasn't the first algorithmic
stablecoin to break.

251
00:19:49,119 --> 00:19:55,183
In June 2021, a project called Iron Finance saw its
partly algorithmic stablecoin lose its peg,

252
00:19:55,183 --> 00:20:01,625
while its sister token fell from around 60
dollars to almost zero in less than a day.

253
00:20:01,875 --> 00:20:06,223
Same design idea. Same spiral. Smaller
scale.

254
00:20:06,773 --> 00:20:09,452
So why does the idea keep coming back?

255
00:20:09,452 --> 00:20:13,846
Because the dream is powerful. Money as
steady as a dollar,

256
00:20:13,846 --> 00:20:16,642
without anyone needing to hold the
dollars.

257
00:20:16,892 --> 00:20:19,152
And because the mechanism works perfectly,

258
00:20:19,152 --> 00:20:24,426
right up until the moment people stop believing in
it. Confidence is the collateral.

259
00:20:24,976 --> 00:20:30,364
And the yield makes the math look like
magic. Run the numbers yourself.

260
00:20:30,364 --> 00:20:32,781
Fourteen billion dollars of deposits,

261
00:20:32,781 --> 00:20:39,547
at nearly 20 percent, means roughly 2.7 billion
dollars a year in promised interest.

262
00:20:39,797 --> 00:20:44,683
Anchor's borrowers never paid anything
close to that. The difference had

263
00:20:44,683 --> 00:20:49,569
to come from somewhere: reserves,
subsidies, and new money coming in.

264
00:20:50,119 --> 00:20:56,067
Lawmakers noticed. In July 2025, the
United States passed the GENIUS Act,

265
00:20:56,067 --> 00:21:03,501
which requires payment stablecoins to be backed one-for-one by
reserves like cash and short-term Treasuries.

266
00:21:04,501 --> 00:21:07,655
This isn't investment advice. It's a
pattern.

267
00:21:07,655 --> 00:21:11,237
When a yield is far above what anything
safe pays,

268
00:21:11,237 --> 00:21:17,327
the money is coming from somewhere. If you can't see
where, it might be coming from you.

269
00:21:18,527 --> 00:21:21,377
Terra didn't fail because nobody warned it
would.

270
00:21:21,377 --> 00:21:25,914
It failed because a 20 percent promise was
more convincing than every warning.

271
00:21:26,914 --> 00:21:30,636
If something promises you high returns
with no risk,

272
00:21:30,636 --> 00:21:34,771
ask one question: where is the money
actually coming from?

273
00:21:35,321 --> 00:21:38,820
Terra was a Korean story the whole world
watched.

274
00:21:38,820 --> 00:21:46,398
Next time: a Korean story the world never heard. A man who
took money from tens of thousands of people,

275
00:21:46,398 --> 00:21:52,461
fled the country, and was then reported dead. Many of
his victims still don't believe it.

276
00:21:53,011 --> 00:21:54,986
Subscribe so you don't miss it.

277
00:21:54,986 --> 00:22:01,040
And tell me in the comments: did you, or someone you
know, ever get caught in a crypto collapse?

